        "original_id": "8af2d28c-dbc6-5b50-8cb4-654b62a3d030",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Camassia, Chelone\n- Places: Camas County, Idaho\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, native ranges, place naming\n\nFacts:\n- Camassia is a genus of plants in the asparagus family that is native to Canada and the United States.\n- Chelone is a genus of four species of perennial herbaceous plants that is native to eastern North America.\n- Camas County, Idaho, is named for the camas root, or Camassia, a lily-like plant with an edible bulb found in the region.\n- Native Americans and settlers used the edible bulb of Camassia as a food source in the region of Camas County, Idaho.",
